      "message": "It looks like this is only used for static executables. I think dynamic executables/libraries would use the unwinder from libc.so instead. The unwinder APIs were added to libc.so starting in R.\n\nI recently removed libgcc_stripped -- do we need to put it back? Maybe it can be restored and only exposed to the VNDK, or exposed as a VNDK snapshot static library? (I was thinking of removing external/libunwind_llvm from the manifest, but I suppose that has the same issue.)\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1663859\n\nIf I\u0027m right that this only affects static executables, then I wonder why we don\u0027t just use the ordinary platform unwinder? (i.e. the libunwind.a prebuilt in prebuilts/clang.) I\u0027d guess that we\u0027re already using the latest libc.a, Clang, builtins library, etc. What libc++/libc++abi is used? I see static libc++ archives in prebuilts/ndk, but I see no static archives at all in prebuilts/vndk.\n",
